            <ArticleTitle>[Sciatic pain and intervertebral disc prolapse after gynecologic operations].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>261-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Among 65 patients operated by lumbar disc in 1977 we encountered 5 women after gynecological tumour operations. 4 of those patients not became symptom free. The relation of mechanical factors, obstruction and circulation changes seemed to be of importance for the evaluation of ischialgia in those cases and led to spinal root and root sheath damages.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
